## Step 3: Launch Two EC2 Web Instances & Verify Directly

Deploy servers into distinct Availability Zones and confirm local web server functionality prior to load balancer attachment.

### Launch Instance 1

1. Navigate to **Launch Templates**, select `web-server-template`, and click **Actions** -> **Launch instance from template**.
2. Configure:
* **Name:** `web-server-1`
* **Subnet:** Select your first available subnet (e.g., `us-east-1a`).
* **Advanced details -> User data:** Replace the placeholder text with:



```bash
#!/bin/bash
dnf update -y
dnf install -y httpd

echo "KeepAlive On" >> /etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf
echo "KeepAliveTimeout 65" >> /etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf

systemctl start httpd
systemctl enable httpd
echo "<h1>Hello from Web Server 1</h1>" > /var/www/html/index.html

```

3. Click **Launch instance**.

### Launch Instance 2

1. Return to **Launch Templates**, select `web-server-template`, and click **Actions** -> **Launch instance from template**.
2. Configure:
* **Name:** `web-server-2`
* **Subnet:** Select a **different** subnet/AZ from Instance 1 (e.g., `us-east-1b`).
* **Advanced details -> User data:** Replace the script with:



```bash
#!/bin/bash
dnf update -y
dnf install -y httpd

echo "KeepAlive On" >> /etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf
echo "KeepAliveTimeout 65" >> /etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf

systemctl start httpd
systemctl enable httpd
echo "<h1>Hello from Web Server 2</h1>" > /var/www/html/index.html

```

3. Click **Launch instance**.

> **Verification Check (Direct Host Test):**
> 1. In **Instances**, wait until both `web-server-1` and `web-server-2` report **Running** and **2/2 checks passed**.
> 2. Copy the **Public IPv4 address** of `web-server-1` into a browser tab (`http://<PUBLIC_IP_1>`). Confirm it renders **"Hello from Web Server 1"**.
> 3. Copy the **Public IPv4 address** of `web-server-2` into a browser tab (`http://<PUBLIC_IP_2>`). Confirm it renders **"Hello from Web Server 2"**.
> 
> 

